    "html": "<p>In a laboratory setup, monochromatic light of wavelength <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"620\\ \\text{nm}\"></span> illuminates a single slit of unknown width. The diffraction pattern is projected onto a screen <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2.5\\ \\text{m}\"></span> away. The angular separation between the first minima on either side of the central maximum is measured to be <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"1.00^\\circ\"></span>. What is the slit width?</p><ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"1.4 \\times 10^{-4} \\text{ m}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"B\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"3.6 \\times 10^{-4} \\text{ m}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"C\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"7.1 \\times 10^{-5} \\text{ m}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"D\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"8.9 \\times 10^{-5} \\text{ m}\"></span></p></li></ol>"
